    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\nCan you configure mini.completion such that C-y (or any configured key) will automatically accept the first suggestion? I find it a bit cumbersome to navigate down to the first suggestion, then accept it. I already use mini.keymap with CR as pmenu_accept.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Can you configure mini.completion such that C-y (or any configured key) will automatically accept the first suggestion? I find it a bit cumbersome to navigate down to the first suggestion, then accept it. I already use mini.keymap with CR as pmenu_accept.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion\nQuestion\nCan you configure mini.completion such that C-y (or any configured key) will automatically accept the first suggestion? I find it a bit cumbersome to navigate down to the first suggestion, then accept it. I already use mini.keymap with CR as pmenu_accept.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-10-02T13:07:20Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, it is possible by using `noinsert` flag in 'completeopt' instead of (suggested) `noselect`. For example, by using the following full value: `vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy,nosort'`. It can be done before or after `require('mini.completion').setup()`, it doesn't matter.\r\n\r\nNote, that this should probably work fine if you want to explicitly select with `<C-y>` or a remap. There might be issues with not applied additional text edits ([it might require selecting an item and wait for a bit](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-completion.txt#L459-L463)), but it might be good enough.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, it is possible by using <code class=\"notranslate\">noinsert</code> flag in 'completeopt' instead of (suggested) <code class=\"notranslate\">noselect</code>. For example, by using the following full value: <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy,nosort'</code>. It can be done before or after <code class=\"notranslate\">require('mini.completion').setup()</code>, it doesn't matter.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note, that this should probably work fine if you want to explicitly select with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-y&gt;</code> or a remap. There might be issues with not applied additional text edits (<a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-completion.txt#L459-L463\">it might require selecting an item and wait for a bit</a>), but it might be good enough.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, it is possible by using noinsert flag in 'completeopt' instead of (suggested) noselect. For example, by using the following full value: vim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy,nosort'. It can be done before or after require('mini.completion').setup(), it doesn't matter.\nNote, that this should probably work fine if you want to explicitly select with <C-y> or a remap. There might be issues with not applied additional text edits (it might require selecting an item and wait for a bit), but it might be good enough.",
